menu "Station: network"

    config NETWORK_AP_SSID_PREFIX
        string "Setup AP SSID prefix"
        default "onocoydiy-"
        help
            The setup access point is named <prefix><last 4 hex digits of MAC>.

    config NETWORK_AP_CHANNEL
        int "Setup AP channel"
        range 1 13
        default 1

    config NETWORK_STA_FALLBACK_S
        int "Seconds without Wi-Fi before the setup AP also comes up"
        range 30 3600
        default 300
        help
            The station keeps retrying its configured network; after this long
            without a connection it additionally starts the setup AP (AP+STA)
            so the user can fix the credentials. The AP stops again a minute
            after the station has an IP (so the setup page can still show the
            new address).

    config NETWORK_RECOVERY_AP_S
        int "Recovery AP lifetime after a BOOT-button press (s)"
        range 120 3600
        default 900
        help
            The AP started by the BOOT button (admin password cleared, or
            settings unreadable) goes down again after this long, or later
            when the last connected client leaves, but at most 30 min after
            this lifetime even while a client stays connected.

    config NETWORK_WIFI_COUNTRY
        string "Wi-Fi country code"
        default "01"
        help
            ISO 3166 alpha-2 code, or "01" for the conservative worldwide
            setting. Sets the allowed channels and transmit power.

    config NETWORK_FALLBACK_DNS1
        string "Fallback DNS server 1"
        default "1.1.1.1"
        help
            Used by the network recovery ladder when the DHCP-provided DNS
            stops answering.

    config NETWORK_FALLBACK_DNS2
        string "Fallback DNS server 2"
        default "9.9.9.9"
        help
            Second server for the same switch. Both are also the targets of
            the upstream probe's TCP check (port 53) when a name lookup
            fails, which tells a DNS failure from no internet at all.

    config NETWORK_PROBE_HOST
        string "Upstream probe host"
        default "github.com"
        help
            Name looked up and connected to (TCP, closed at once, nothing
            sent) by the upstream probe, which tells "no IP" from "IP but no
            upstream" for the network recovery ladder. The default is a host
            the station talks to anyway (update check). Never a caster: a
            bare connect could count as a failed source login there.

    config NETWORK_PROBE_PORT
        int "Upstream probe TCP port"
        range 1 65535
        default 443

    config NETWORK_QEMU_ETHERNET
        bool "QEMU development build: emulated Ethernet instead of Wi-Fi"
        depends on ETH_USE_OPENETH
        default y
        help
            For running the firmware in Espressif's QEMU only (the overlay
            sdkconfig.qemu at the repository root, tools/qemu/run.sh). It
            can only be turned on together with the OpenCores Ethernet MAC
            driver (ETH_USE_OPENETH), which exists in QEMU and on no real
            chip, and never with the defaults a station is built from.

            Wi-Fi is never initialised or started (QEMU has no radio). The
            emulated Ethernet port takes the station interface's place:
            same interface key and IP events, link up and down reported as
            the station's association, DHCP from QEMU's user-mode network.
            There is no setup AP. The web server accepts the Host names
            localhost and 127.0.0.1 (QEMU's port forward) and treats every
            request as if it came over the setup AP, so the first admin
            password can be set from the development machine.

            Configure refuses a release build with this option, and the
            release job refuses to publish one.

endmenu
